Package: eyetrajectories
Title: Functional Analysis of Eye-Tracking Trajectories
Version: 0.4.3.9000
Authors@R: person("Stefanos", "Balaskas", email = "s.balaskas@ac.upatras.gr", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides native R tools for time-indexed eye-tracking
    trajectories, including validation, explicit preprocessing, kinematics,
    trajectory distances, functional principal component analysis, multivariate
    functional principal component analysis and recurrence diagnostics.
    Includes experimental sparse and multilevel functional methods and
    participant-level resampling with documented methodological restrictions.
    An optional interface to the Python package 'eyetrajectoriespy' is
    available through 'reticulate'; native R methods do not require Python.
    Availability of an interface does not imply numerical equivalence between
    implementations.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/stefanosbalaskas/eyetrajectories
